@reactions favour
// Writer-commons, reactions (reworked). A favour you did (social's cue favour.lamp | favour.fetch | favour.job; every
// favour is .you). @me: the person you helped, the next day. Without @me: someone who heard about it.

? cue:favour.lamp.you@me
- My lamp's still going. Every night I switch it on and think, that was {me}.   #warm
- I can read in bed again. You've no idea. {thanks}.
? cue:favour.fetch.you@me
- {thanks} for fetching that yesterday. Saved my legs and my temper.
- You went all that way for me. I owe you a tea. Two teas.   #warm
? cue:favour.job.you@me
- That little job you did for me? Still perfect. {thanks}. Really.
- I keep telling people you helped me out. They're sick of hearing it.   #funny
? cue:favour.you@me tier>=friend
- You didn't have to help yesterday. You just did. That's you, isn't it.   #warm

? cue:favour.you !cue:favour.you@me
- I hear you helped someone out yesterday. That's the Wren way.   #warm
- Word gets round on a ship this size. Good word, about you.
- I hear you did someone a favour. It comes back round. It always does.
? cue:favour.you !cue:favour.you@me tier>=friend
- Heard what you did. Typical you. Don't let them take advantage, mind.   #warm
? cue:favour.you !cue:favour.you@me dept:galley
- Heard you've been helping people. Come and get a biscuit. That's how it works here.   #warm
? cue:favour.you !cue:favour.you@me dept:store
- Heard you've been doing favours. I've seen your ledger. You've earned a cheap tea.   #funny

// Writer 4, batch 9: more favours (Commons voices).
? cue:favour.you@me tier>=acquaintance
- I owe you one. Well. I owe you a pudding.   #funny
- {thanks} again for yesterday. Made my whole day easier.
? cue:favour.you@me dept:garden
- Mm. Yesterday. {thanks}. The beans noticed too.   #funny
? cue:favour.you !cue:favour.you@me dept:infirmary
- Heard you helped someone out. Good for the heart, that is.   #warm
? cue:favour.you !cue:favour.you@me rank:junior
- Bunk's buzzing. You helped someone. Nice one.
? cue:favour.you !cue:favour.you@me
- Somebody did a kind thing yesterday. I heard who.   #warm
